WEBVTT

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.900
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:31.240
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:38.980
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:45.120
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.890
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:57.600
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:04.580
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:12.510
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:20.180
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.430
And now, for the weather.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.600
Yes, I realize you're busy, but...

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.200
"Tokyo Tower, B1 Control Room"

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:32.500
In the Kanto region, a low pressure system...

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.840
No, it is working today...

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.070
...but it's been acting up.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.180
It just completely stopped moving.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.810
...will bring rains for the afternoon.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.450
It wasn't for long, but still.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.310
Strong winds will blow across Japan today.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.870
It's really worrying me, so
I hope you'll come soon.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.120
You've got to hurry.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.850
People are advised to take special
precautions if going outdoors.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.060
The wind is getting
stronger.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.460
Maybe the tower will
close down today.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.200
Well, it's probably better anyway, the
way the elevator's been acting up.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:29.220
FILE. 34
A 250-METER-
HIGH HOLIDAY

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.370
Winds will be particularly strong
in Tokyo late this afternoon.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.340
"Sumida River"
Winds will be particularly strong
in Tokyo late this afternoon.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:41.390
Winds will be particularly strong
in Tokyo late this afternoon.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:46.210
And now for the regional
weather.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.940
<i>"Day off?"</i>

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.450
<i>"Yeah."</i>

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.310
<i>"But I don't have</i>
<i>anything to do."</i>

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.680
<i>"My wife says I get in the way, so</i>
<i>she doesn't want me at home."</i>

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.560
<i>"I don't have that</i>
<i>problem."</i>

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.060
<i>"Really? What are</i>
<i>you going to do?"</i>

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.060
<i>"Maybe I'll go get</i>
<i>some fresh air..."</i>

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:14.040
<i>Or maybe indoors.</i>

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.220
"Metropolitan Station"

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.730
The advantage of air surveillance is that
it speeds up the capture process.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.930
They could've just sent us a video of this.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:41.700
Firsthand experience is important.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.470
This is called "search and catch" in the
United States; air units are used...

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.940
Anyway, sometimes this training pairs
us with nice guys from headquarters.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.170
...to relay important information about
a pursuit to those on the ground.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.070
Nice guys, huh?

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.650
In a typical operation, information on a suspect...

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.510
...gathered by air surveillance is relayed to...

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:59.680
Come on guys, you should
be paying attention.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.240
...the ground to assist in the capture.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.760
The key to success is good communications...

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.460
We may have to go back
before we're done.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.330
...between airborne and ground units.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:13.820
The winds have really
picked up today.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.270
Hello? This is the elevator
control room.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.070
The wind's blowing over
19 meters per second.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.650
Yes, that's right.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.740
I hear it's going
to get worse.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.080
Yes.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.780
Close off the top?

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:37.760
Yes, sir.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.620
"Upper Observation Deck Announcements"
"Strong Winds" "Emergencies" "Closing"

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:49.660
Thank you for visiting
Tokyo Tower today.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.440
Your attention please.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.830
We apologize for the inconvenience, but due
to the unusually strong winds today...

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:02.000
...the upper observation deck
will now be closing.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.010
Would everyone please proceed
to the elevator...

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.120
...and leave the upper observation
deck immediately.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.390
We apologize for the inconvenience, but due
to the unusually strong winds today...

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.190
You can feel the sway. It's getting
pretty windy out there.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:18.180
...the upper observation deck
will now be closing.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.260
You'd better get in line
at the elevator.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:20.970
Would everyone please proceed
to the elevator...

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.370
I'll be done when I'm finished.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.000
...and leave the upper observation
deck immediately.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.260
I'm still investigating. Don't bug me.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.800
Still investigating? What
are you talking about?

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:31.960
Great, my time's up.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.300
Me?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.780
I'm a member of the Tokyo
Investigation Club.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:37.280
"Tokyo Investigation Club"

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.080
Oh?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:39.220
"Tokyo Investigation Club"

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.240
See this symbol?

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:40.250
"Tokyo Investigation Club"

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.080
It's a Japanese
wolf. Right?

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.550
Y... Yeah, that's right.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.320
Oh, no!

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.070
My friends and I created it.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.030
The Tokyo Investigation
Club, huh?

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:06.510
Yeah. It's a race to see who
can spot a big crime.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.480
Oh... Think you'll see anything
from way up here?

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.140
I see.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:14.440
Where are your
friends?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.850
Down below. On the lower
observation deck.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:20.420
That's quite the thing, coming
here after school.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:21.650
What about you?

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.550
Well... Hmm...

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.530
It's a weekday. What
about work?

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.260
Oh, I get it! You
were laid off!

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:34.200
Don't give up, you'll find
something soon.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.200
Shall we get going?

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.210
Somebody stole it! You've
got to find him!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.110
So it was your purse
that you lost?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.470
That's right.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.710
I wanted to look through the telescope,
so I put my purse down right there.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.050
But I just left it there
a moment.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:51.720
Hey!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.550
I had everything in it.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.730
How long has it been since you
first noticed it was missing?

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.460
Two or three minutes.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:07.440
I don't have any identification on me, so
you just have to trust me. I'm a cop.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.440
Here, let me give
you my card.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.470
Hey, you're a
cop! Cool!

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.470
That's wonderful.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:17.710
Will you be able
to help us out?

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.110
It's almost certainly
a sneak thief.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.690
The culprit is probably
still up here.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:26.220
Ah... I see.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.860
Thank you.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.120
Excuse me, ladies
and gentlemen.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:36.190
I'm afraid we have a small problem.
I need to ask for your cooperation.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.730
Stay here and watch.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:39.960
This won't take long.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.430
This is a crime, isn't
it?! All right!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.640
It's not a game, son.
Stay here.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.080
The wind's up to 20
meters per second.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.840
We're heading
back.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.780
Then I won't be able
to write my report.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.420
Let's go back. I'm going
to throw up.

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:00.160
What?

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:07.050
Thank you for your
cooperation.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:35.180
Stop!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.130
Wait! Calm down!

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.690
Wait a second,
driver!

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.230
He's called a pilot.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:42.830
The Chief's over there!

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.670
Huh? He is?

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.790
He is?

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.990
He's on the upper observation
deck of Tokyo Tower!

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.040
I can't see him.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:00.150
I wonder what he's doing at Tokyo
Tower on his day off?

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.910
He's running,
that's what.

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.050
Huh?

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.150
Damn!

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.790
Don't move!

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.100
I thought I told you to
stay where you were.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:26.400
Uh... yeah...

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.000
Something's going on down there.
I think the Chief's in trouble.

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.470
Driver, get in a
little closer.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.700
I can't. We've got to go back.
This wind is too strong.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.970
Forget that!

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.180
What's going on?!

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:13.320
Give me your key. I come here
a lot. I know the place.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.630
What are you talking about?!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:15.960
Don't play games with me.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.030
Give me the key to the outside
stairs. Make it fast!

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:23.520
You fool! The reason the
tower is closing down...

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:27.000
...is because the wind's blowing over
20 meters per second outside.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:29.000
You'll be risking
your life!

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:31.510
You know everything.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.140
I live nearby. I come
here a lot.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:48.150
Wait. Listen to me. You have no idea
how dangerous that wind is.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:51.090
Quiet! Open the door!

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.570
Don't do it!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.220
Huh?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:29.590
Help me!

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.700
Damn! This is one day off
I'm not going to forget.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.770
Don't do it! Chief!
Get back inside!

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:56.580
Help! Please help me!

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.690
Whatever you do, don't look down!
Head for the door! Come on!

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.330
Come on! Run for it!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:12.530
Hurry, mister!

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:13.970
Oh, no!

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:16.270
Hey! Get down
from there!

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:25.780
This is bad!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.080
Hurry!

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.400
Watch out, son!

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:23.560
It's no use.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.210
That last gust warped
the door.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:00.540
All right. From now on, you've got
to listen to me very carefully.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.270
Are you listening?

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.750
If you're listening,
answer me.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:12.880
Yeah... I'm listening.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.320
Good.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.120
This is our situation.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:23.030
That door is stuck, and there's no way
we'll be able to open it from here.

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:26.730
To make matters worse, I've
twisted my right ankle...

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.800
...and it... it hurts!

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:34.870
We're 250 meters
off the ground.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:42.880
It's not bad right now, but the wind
is going to get a lot stronger.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:47.050
Since there's no prevailing direction,
there's nowhere to hide.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:50.220
We're sitting ducks.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:52.620
What's your name?

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.390
Ryousuke Shiroyama.

00:15:56.570 --> 00:16:03.840
Ryousuke. We've got to stay calm.
You need to believe in yourself.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.140
Huh?

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:14.740
You need to believe that we're going
to be okay... can you do that?

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:19.050
I... l'll try.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.820
Attaboy.

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:34.740
What?! What the
hell is going on?

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:43.210
This is Kobayakawa of the Bokuto
Station Traffic Section...

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:47.240
...calling the Emergency
Information Center.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:50.720
We have an emergency. Repeat...
We have an emergency.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:55.720
We have two people stranded outside
on the upper deck of Tokyo Tower.

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:58.850
Immediate assistance is needed,
due to the strong winds.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:01.260
Roger.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:14.740
We request all available
resources.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.980
That's the situation.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:22.820
Tsujimoto and Kobayakawa are on the
scene, and are requesting a rescue.

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:26.150
But the Chief...

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:27.390
"Traffic Section, Section Chief"

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:29.890
What was he doing
up there?

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:30.560
"Traffic Section, Section Chief"

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.130
He wanted to get
some fresh air.

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:34.730
Huh?

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.930
Listen up. I want you
to move quickly.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:42.230
We don't know how long the Chief
and that kid can hold on.

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:50.380
I want them rescued before the wind
blows them right off the tower.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:53.810
But, Detective, it's out
of our jurisdiction.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:59.150
Wait and see. He's our
guy, so we'll save him.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.790
That's the way we did things
when I was your age.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.160
All officers will proceed to
the Shiba Zojoji Temple.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:10.260
We will mount a rescue together with
the emergency rescue squad.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:12.700
Get moving!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:15.710
"Operations Center, Zojoji Temple"

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:21.740
Yes, that's right. Yes. You go like this...
This goes here... That is correct.
"Operations Center, Zojoji Temple"

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:24.510
Yes. Hello...

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:28.750
It's good to have all these people working
on it, but I feel so useless!

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.790
Can't be helped. It's out
of our jurisdiction.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:34.750
But we can still do our
best to cooperate.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:36.550
Yeah.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:43.390
Detective Tokuno and the others left
the station! They're on the way!

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:44.900
Great!

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:45.800
Great!
What?

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:47.870
You can't carry out
the rescue!

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.340
What are you saying?
Huh?

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.010
I'll call you
later.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.940
This wind is wreaking havoc
all over the place.

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:03.710
They won't be able to
get here for awhile.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.350
So you're going to
just leave them?

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:07.390
Natsumi!

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:09.820
Hello...

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:11.320
...are you from Bokuto
Station?

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:14.090
Yes. Yes, we are.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:16.660
What?!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.660
The elevator's broken?!

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:20.300
Y... Yes.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:23.040
Once all the other people
got down...

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.510
...we thought of using a blow-
torch on the jammed door.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:27.310
Oh, no!

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.410
It's been acting up since
this morning.

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:31.550
I'm very sorry.

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:36.910
The elevator's out, so there's no way
to take any equipment up to the top.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:43.420
There are outer stairs to
the observation deck...

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.760
...but in this wind, it would
be far too dangerous.

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:55.170
Getting hungry, son?

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:59.440
Huh? Is this any time
for small talk?

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:05.010
You have to eat well, just in case
something like this happens.

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.220
A helicopter! They're
coming to rescue us!

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:17.790
No, they're not.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.260
No, they're not.
Huh?!

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.060
They're just checking us out.
Huh?!

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.460
They can't get any closer
in this wind.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.570
It's amazing that they're
still flying.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:31.470
How can you stay
so calm, mister?

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.410
Real men keep
their cool.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.010
Huh?

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:50.650
I understand that this is outside
our jurisdiction.

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:58.290
Yes. I've just got to save
my friend. Thank you.

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:02.900
I'll be indebted
to you for life.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:06.000
Yes. Thank you
very much.

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:16.720
Tokuno just called in.

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:20.410
Bokuto Station is... Bokuto Station's
going to handle the whole thing.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:23.130
Everything! All of it!

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:45.740
All this fresh air is starting
to get to me.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:22:00.730
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:11.340
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:18.240
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:28.360
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.420 --> 00:22:42.330
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:50.610
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:59.190
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:07.220
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.330 --> 00:23:16.800
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:24.280
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:27.740
"Tsujimoto, c'mon!"

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:30.520
A major low pressure system
is approaching...

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:34.020
...with wind speeds over
30 meters per second!

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:37.520
Oh, no! That's like a
typhoon, isn't it?!

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:41.160
Tsujimoto, this man here
will help you out.

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:46.030
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 35...

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:48.240
..."Friendship at 250 Meters."

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:50.240
Who the heck are you?
